{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Turing-Acceptable Language.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Turing-Acceptable Language.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"turing acceptable language turing acceptable language","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Turing-Acceptable Language.md","fileName":"Turing-Acceptable Language.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Turing-Acceptable Language","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 22:54\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Turing Machines and Computability]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Turing Machines and Computability","Turing Machine","Turing-Decidable Language","Recursively Enumerable Language","FoundationsOfComputation_2.3.2.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Turing-Acceptable Language.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Turing-Acceptable Language.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"turing acceptable language turing acceptable language","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Turing-Acceptable Language.md","fileName":"Turing-Acceptable Language.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Turing-Acceptable Language","heading":"Turing-Acceptable Language","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A language is Turing-acceptable when some [[Turing Machine]] halts exactly on the strings in the language. For a string outside the language, the machine may run forever rather than halt with an explicit rejection.\n\nEvery [[Turing-Decidable Language|decidable language]] is acceptable, but the converse fails. Turing-acceptable languages are exactly the [[Recursively Enumerable Language|recursively enumerable languages]] and exactly the languages generated by general grammars.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Turing Machines and Computability","Turing Machine","Turing-Decidable Language","Recursively Enumerable Language","FoundationsOfComputation_2.